{
  "description": "Test vectors for program.json progression rules. Each case is one slot, the sessions logged for it oldest first, and the target an implementation should work out next. A session gives its top working load and each working set's reps in order (or holds, in seconds, for timed sets), and the exercise it was logged as when that isn't the slot's own; null reps or holds are unknown. A percent_of_slot case gives reference, the current target of the slot it reads (a load, or needs_start), in place of sessions. Missing data holds: a session with unknown reps on a set the rule reads is neither a success nor a miss, unless a set is missing or another set was logged short. want.loads lists each set group's weight, in order, when the slot's set groups carry their own percent of the training max. want.exercise is the exercise to do next, for a variations rule. Exercise IDs illustrate the rules and aren't checked against the catalogue. Loads are in the case's unit. A reduced load is rounded down to step for that unit, and an increment in another unit is converted and rounded to it. Explanations are each app's own words and aren't part of the vectors.",
